{#
  /llms-full.txt — llms.txt with the pages' full text inline (see _views/feeds/llms.twig
  for the format, the text/plain type and why autoescape is off).

  llms.txt is the map: a model reads it and follows links. This is the territory, so
  one fetch is enough to answer from — every live case study, note, tool and page, in
  the order llms.txt lists them, notes newest first and ALL of them rather than ten.

  Bodies are the same fields the pages render, converted from their HTML by
  craft.frontend.markdown(): `content` (about, policy pages) and the caseContent
  blocks (case studies, notes, tools). Only blocks that carry words are written out —
  images, video and lottie have nothing for a model to read, and the homepage
  analysis form is a form. A quote is written as a quote with its attribution, code
  as a fenced block, and the method block as the methodology's phases.
#}
{%- header "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8" -%}
{%- set about = craft.entries().section('about').status('live').one() -%}
{%- set caseStudyIndex = craft.entries().section('caseStudy').status('live').one() -%}
{%- set notesIndex = craft.entries().section('note').status('live').one() -%}
{%- set contact = craft.entries().section('contact').status('live').one() -%}
{%- set tools = craft.entries().section('tools').status('live').all() -%}
{%- set studies = craft.entries().section('caseStudies').status('live').all() -%}
{%- set notes = craft.entries().section('notes').status('live').orderBy('postDate DESC').all() -%}
{%- set pages = craft.entries().section('pages').status('live').all() -%}
{#- Autoescape INSIDE each macro — a macro escapes in the context it was defined in,
    not where it's called (see llms.twig). -#}
{%- macro line(text) -%}
    {%- autoescape false -%}
        {{- (text ?? '')|striptags|split("\n\n")|first|trim|replace({"\n": ' ', "\r": ''}) -}}
    {%- endautoescape -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro blocks(entry) -%}
    {%- autoescape false -%}
    {%- for block in entry.caseContent.all() ?? [] -%}
        {%- set handle = block.type.handle -%}
        {%- if handle == 'content' -%}
            {%- set md = craft.frontend.markdown(block.content ?? '') -%}
            {%- if md %}{{ md }}

{% endif -%}
        {%- elseif handle == 'code' and (block.codeSnippet ?? '')|trim -%}
```{{ block.codeLanguage ?? '' }}
{{ block.codeSnippet|trim }}
```

{% elseif handle == 'caseTestimonial' -%}
            {%- set quoted = block.testimonial.status(null).one() -%}
            {%- if quoted and (quoted.blockquote ?? '')|trim -%}
                {%- set who = [quoted.personName ?? '', quoted.jobTitle ?? '', craft.frontend.testimonialCompany(quoted)]|map(v => v|trim)|filter(v => v)|join(', ') -%}
> {{ quoted.blockquote|striptags|trim|replace({"\n\n": "\n>\n> ", "\n": "\n> "}) }}
{% if who %}>
> — {{ who }}
{% endif %}

{% endif -%}
        {%- elseif handle == 'contentMethod' -%}
            {%- for phase in craft.frontend.methodology() -%}
**{{ phase.title }}**{% if phase.summary %}: {{ phase.summary|striptags|trim }}{% endif %}{% if phase.services|length %} ({{ phase.services|join(', ') }}){% endif %}

{% endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endautoescape -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- import _self as f -%}
{#- ONE BLANK LINE BETWEEN THINGS, enforced on the whole output rather than tag by tag.
    A block that prints nothing (an image, a video) still leaves its line breaks, and
    the trim markers to stop that are a game of whack-a-mole across a dozen branches. -#}
{% autoescape false %}
{% apply replace('/\\n{3,}/', "\n\n", true) %}
# {{ siteName }}

> {{ f.line(about.summary ?? '') ?: 'Design, development and maintenance of digital products.' }}

The full text of {{ siteUrl() }} in one file. The short index, with a line per page, is
{{ siteUrl('llms.txt') }}. The homepage has an assistant that answers questions about
the work in Jon's own voice; everything it draws on is below.

{% if about %}
## {{ about.title }}

Source: {{ about.url }}

{% set body = craft.frontend.markdown(about.content ?? '') -%}
{% if body %}{{ body }}

{% endif %}
{{- f.blocks(about) }}
{%- endif %}
{%- for tool in tools %}

## {{ tool.title }}

Source: {{ tool.url }}

{% if f.line(tool.summary ?? '') %}{{ f.line(tool.summary ?? '') }}

{% endif %}
{{- f.blocks(tool) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if studies|length %}

# Case studies

{% for study in studies %}
{%- set client = craft.frontend.caseStudyClientName(study, true) -%}
{%- set role = study.skills.all()|map(s => s.title)|join(', ') -%}
{%- set year = (study.hasDateHidden ?? false) or not study.postDate ? '' : study.postDate|date('Y') ~ ((study.isPresent ?? false) ? ' – present' : '') -%}
{%- set sectors = study.sectorSelector.all()|map(c => (c.longTitle ?? '')|trim ?: c.title)|join(', ') -%}
## {{ (study.longTitle ?? '')|trim ?: study.title }}

Source: {{ study.url }}
{% if client %}Client: {{ client }}
{% endif %}
{%- if role %}Role: {{ role }}
{% endif %}
{%- if year %}Year: {{ year }}
{% endif %}
{%- if sectors %}Sectors: {{ sectors }}
{% endif %}

{% set summary = craft.frontend.markdown(study.caseSummary ?? '') -%}
{% if summary %}{{ summary }}

{% endif %}
{{- f.blocks(study) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if notes|length %}

# Notes

{{ f.line(notesIndex.summary ?? '') }}

{% for note in notes %}
{%- set topics = note.topicSelector is defined ? note.topicSelector.all()|map(t => t.title)|join(', ') : '' -%}
## {{ note.title }}

Source: {{ note.url }}
{% if note.postDate %}Published: {{ note.postDate|date('Y-m-d') }}
{% endif %}
{%- if topics %}Topics: {{ topics }}
{% endif %}

{% set summary = f.line(note.summary ?? '') -%}
{% if summary %}{{ summary }}

{% endif %}
{{- f.blocks(note) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- for page in pages %}

## {{ page.title }}

Source: {{ page.url }}
{% set body = craft.frontend.markdown(page.content ?? '') -%}
{% if body %}

{{ body }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{%- if contact %}

## {{ contact.title }}

Source: {{ contact.url }}

The contact page has a form, and the homepage assistant can take a message too.
{% endif %}
{% endapply %}
{% endautoescape %}
